    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0727" n="1236" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg1236"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/7–2348</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Telephone Conversation, by the Director of
                        the Office of United Nations Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Rusk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-07-23">July 23, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Ohly<anchor n="1" xml:id="d479-f1"/> called and said that the War Council
                    (Secretary of Defense and Secretaries of the Army, Navy and Air Force) had been
                    briefed by Mr. Bohlen on the Palestine situation and had come to the following
                    conclusion, subject to the views of the Joint Chiefs of Staff: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>That the maintenance of the truce in Palestine was of vital interest
                            to the security of the United States;</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>That the United States should do everything we properly can to help
                            Count Bernadotte implement the truce;</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>That instructions should be issued to Admiral Sherman to see Count
                            Bernadotte immediately to work out an observation plan and a program of
                            United States assistance;</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>That consideration should be given as to whether the whole job of
                            assistance should be turned over to a single service or should be
                            continued on an inter-service basis.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d479-f1" n="1" xml:id="d479-f1-content">
                <p>John H. Ohly, Special Assistant to the Secretary of Defense.</p>
            </note>
